{"title":"Naoki Sato","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p><b>Naoki Sato</b> is the director of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Worldwide_Online_Olympiad_Training\" title=\"Worldwide Online Olympiad Training\">Worldwide Online Olympiad Training</a> program and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Art_of_Problem_Solving\" title=\"Art of Problem Solving\">Art of Problem Solving</a> instructor.  His career as a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mathematics\" title=\"Mathematics\">mathematics</a> educator and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mathematics_competition\" title=\"Mathematics competition\">mathematics competition</a> champion include the following:\n</p>\n<ul><li>Three-time deputy director of the Canadian <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=International_Mathematical_Olympiad\" title=\"International Mathematical Olympiad\">International Mathematical Olympiad</a> (IMO) team</li>\n<li>Silver and bronze medals at the IMO</li>\n<li>Winner of the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Canadian_Mathematical_Olympiad\" title=\"Canadian Mathematical Olympiad\">Canadian Mathematical Olympiad</a></li>\n<li>Masters degree in Mathematics from <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Yale_University\" title=\"Yale University\">Yale University</a></li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Naoki_Sato&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Fundamental_Theorem_of_Sato\" title=\"Fundamental Theorem of Sato\">Fundamental Theorem of Sato</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018004017\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.005 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.006 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 10/1000000\nPost‐expand